# A damaged file (an extension): a sketch placed on a point the file
# lacks is left out, and the reference workplanes it lacks are put back;
# a chamfer's edge the file lacks is left out of the chamfer and kept;
# a lathe's axis and a mirror's plane it lacks leave the group out.
# A message says so on opening, and Features > Broken References lists each,
# with what can take the place of what the file lacks.
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/group_missing_workplane.tlspr
tw
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/missing_references.tlspr
tw
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/chamfer_missing_edge.tlspr
tw
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
# A diameter whose circle the file lacks: the circle is named for its
# kind. An extrusion whose sketch the file lacks: [choose a group] lists
# the model's groups to take its place.
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/constraint_missing_circle.tlspr
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/group_missing_operand.tlspr
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
click-tw [choose a group]
tw
# A lathe whose axis the file lacks and a mirror whose plane it lacks:
# each is named for the kind that can take its place.
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/lathe_missing_axis.tlspr
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
answer ok
load tlspr/damaged/mirror_missing_plane.tlspr
menu Features|Broken References...
tw
